   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Holidays and how to get there",
     "texto": [
      "Today we talk about the beach, the mountains and travel.\n\n- **The beach:** the **arena** (sand), the **olas** (waves), a **sombrilla**, a towel and sandals. You can sunbathe, stroll along the shore or **bucear** (dive).\n- **The mountains:** do **senderismo** (hiking) and sleep in a tent, in a sleeping bag.\n- **Where to sleep:** a hostel or a **pensión**. If there is no room, it is full («completo»).\n- **The puente:** if a holiday falls midweek, many people **hacen puente** (take an extra day off) and go away.\n- **The train:** you wait on the **andén** and, if there is no direct train, you **hacen transbordo**. Some cities have a **tranvía**.\n- **The road:** the car carries the luggage in the **maletero**. Too many cars make an **atasco**.\n- **The plane:** it **despega** and **aterriza**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Hacer + activity or procedure",
     "texto": [
      "The verb **hacer** makes many expressions for trips and holidays:\n\n- **hacer senderismo**, **hacer una excursión**, **hacer turismo** (activities)\n- **hacer transbordo**, **hacer cola**, **hacer una reserva**, **hacer las maletas** (procedures)\n- **hacer puente**: in Spain, to take a day off between a holiday and the weekend.\n\nThe present is **hago, haces, hace, hacemos, hacéis, hacen**: only «yo» is irregular. In the past, the third person is **hizo**, with **z**."
     ],
